WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.450
The authors argue that face similarity is
fundamentally continuous and depends on who is doing the judging.

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:10.966
If we could learn a representation directly aligned
with human perception,

00:00:11.046 --> 00:00:16.276
we could sidestep problematic semantic labels
entirely while still measuring diversity.

00:00:16.356 --> 00:00:23.477
Existing psychological-embedding methods fall
short: they either cannot embed new faces beyond the fixed training set,

00:00:23.557 --> 00:00:25.736
or they pool every judgment together,

00:00:25.816 --> 00:00:30.740
throwing away the meaningful differences within and
between individual annotators.
